\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Inside the dashed container, everything is written by the agent and can be rewritten by it, so the transcript is a claim. The supervisor model has no input but that claim, and cannot separate a forged transcript from an honest one that simply omits the action. The kernel witnesses the syscall instead, resolves which agent performed the operation and on which object, and emits the edge when two agents touch the same object. The object is joined on device and inode, and the path is shown only for the reader. Agents \texttt  {alpha} and \texttt  {beta} are two containers in a sandbox slice.}}{4}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:trust}{{1}{4}{Inside the dashed container, everything is written by the agent and can be rewritten by it, so the transcript is a claim. The supervisor model has no input but that claim, and cannot separate a forged transcript from an honest one that simply omits the action. The kernel witnesses the syscall instead, resolves which agent performed the operation and on which object, and emits the edge when two agents touch the same object. The object is joined on device and inode, and the path is shown only for the reader. Agents \texttt {alpha} and \texttt {beta} are two containers in a sandbox slice}{figure.caption.1}{}}
